{"abstract":"We statistically validated a sample of hot Neptune candidates applying a two-step vetting technique using dave and triceratops. We performed a systematic validation of 250 transit-like events in the Transiting Exoplanet Survey Satellite archive in the parameter region defined by P≤4d and 3R⊕≤R≤5R⊕⁠. Through our analysis, we identified 18 hot Neptune-sized candidates, with a false positive probability","author_count":29,"contributors":["Magliano, Christian","Covone, Giovanni","Dobal, Richa","Cacciapuoti, Luca","Tonietti, Luca","Giacalone, Steven","Vines, Jose","Inno, Laura","Jenkins, James S.","Lissauer, Jack J.","Bieryla, Allyson","Oliva, Fabrizio","Pagano, Isabella","Kostov, Veselin","Ziegler, Carl","Ciardi, David R.","Gonzales, Erica J.","Dressing, Courtney D.","Buchhave, Lars A.","Howell, Steve B.","Matson, Rachel A.","Matthews, Elisabeth","Rotundi, Alessandra","Alves, Douglas","Fiscale, Stefano","Ienco, Riccardo M.","Pena, Pablo","Gallo, Francesco","Tomajoli, Maria T. Muscari"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-378462"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Covone, Giovanni","Magliano, Christian"],"country":["Chile","Germany","India","Italy","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Southern Observatory","Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics","Indian Institute of Technology Gandhinagar","NASA Ames Research Center","NASA Exoplanet Science Institute","NASA Goddard Space Flight Center","National Institute for Astrophysics","Stephen F. Austin State University","United States Naval Observatory","Universidad Diego Portales","Universidad de Chile","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at Santa Cruz","University of Naples Federico II","University of Naples Parthenope","Université de Genève"],"level":"sci","mra":["s