"papaleopau","last":"Papaleo","locid":"55479982-b8f2-4e7c-b8be-9230d8fb4767","name":"Papaleo, Elena","orcid":"0000-0003-2296-898X","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniela","key":"deziopau","last":"De Zio","name":"De Zio, Daniela","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Apolinar","key":"mayamendozapau","last":"Maya-Mendoza","name":"Maya-Mendoza, Apolinar","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Franco","key":"locatellipau","last":"Locatelli","name":"Locatelli, Franco","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jiri","key":"bartekpau","last":"Bartek","name":"Bartek, Jiri","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Francesco","key":"cecconipau","last":"Cecconi","name":"Cecconi, Francesco","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33854232"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-021-03422-5","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"journal":"Nature","pages":"799-803","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"592"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104673616"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-69c13cd4-1123-401d-a8b4-ec545e84e73a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"AMBRA1 regulates cyclin D to guard S-phase entry and genomic integrity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-456601","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"River discharge is an important variable to measure in order to predict droughts and flood occurrences. Once the cross-sectional geometry of the river is known, discharge can be inferred from water level and surface flow velocity measurements. Since river discharges are of particular interest during extreme weather events, when river sites cannot be safely accessed, noncontact sensing technologies are particularly appealing. To this purpose, this work proposes a prototype of a low-cost continuous wave (CW) Doppler radar sensor, which is able to monitor the surface flow velocity of rivers. The prototype is tested at two gauged sites in central Italy, along the Tiber River. The surface flow velocity distribution across the river is monitored by means of the analysis of received Doppler signal. The surface velocity statistics are then extracted using a novel algorithm that is optimized to run on a microprocessor platform with minimal computing power (ArduinoUNO). In particular, the radar measurements are used to initialize a 2-D entropy-based velocity model (EVM) that is able to estimate river discharges in any flow condition. Finally, the results concerning the observed discharge provided by the EVM prove to be comparable with those obtained with more expensive commercial solutions. The results are important since the described methodology can be extended to small-size Doppler radar sensors onboard unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), the latter providing a method for mapping surface velocity of rivers.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Alimenti, Federico","Bonafoni, Stefania","Gallo, Elisa","Palazzi, Valentina","Gatti, Roberto Vencenti","Mezzanotte, Paolo","Roselli, Luca","Zito, Domenico","Barbetta, Silvia","Corradini, Christiano","Termini, Donnatella","Moramarco, Tommaso"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-242338"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Research Council","University of Perugia"],"keyword":["River hydraulics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"noncontact measurement of river surface velocity and discharge estimation with a low cost doppler radar sensor","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85087452592","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-242338","identifier":[{"id":"85087452592","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c5edb776-839e-4299-882a-2a1b40ee8884"],"keyword":["Discharge estimation","Doppler centroid estimation","low-cost Doppler radar sensors","river hydraulics","surface velocity radars (SVRs)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-69177E74286D8487660AC0F17B0C2D11"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of perugia","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Perugia","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Wireless Transceivers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"national research council","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Federico","key":"alimentipau","last":"Alimenti","name":"Alimenti, Federico","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefania","key":"bonafonipau","last":"Bonafoni","name":"Bonafoni, Stefania","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"gallopau","last":"Gallo","name":"Gallo, Elisa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina","key":"palazzipau","last":"Palazzi","name":"Palazzi, Valentina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto Vencenti","key":"gattipau","last":"Gatti","name":"Gatti, Roberto Vencenti","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"mezzanottepau","last":"Mezzanotte","name":"Mezzanotte, Paolo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rosellipau","last":"Roselli","name":"Roselli, Luca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Domenico","key":"zitopau","last":"Zito","locid":"0fbf055e-173c-4f96-8f07-6d7e26a2956c","name":"Zito, Domenico","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvia","key":"barbettapau","last":"Barbetta","name":"Barbetta, Silvia","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christiano","key":"corradinipau","last":"Corradini","name":"Corradini, Christiano","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Donnatella","key":"terminipau","last":"Termini","name":"Termini, Donnatella","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tommaso","key":"moramarcopau","last":"Moramarco","name":"Moramarco, Tommaso","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tgrs.2020.2974185","issn":["01962892","15580644"],"issn_org":["01962892"],"issue":"7","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing","pages":"5195-5207","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087452592"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c5edb776-839e-4299-882a-2a1b40ee8884"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Noncontact Measurement of River Surface Velocity and Discharge Estimation With a Low-Cost Doppler Radar Sensor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-242338","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Italian heavy pig selection programs are based on production (average daily gain, ADG; feed gain ratio, FGR), carcass (weight of lean cuts, LC; ham weight, HW; backfat thickness, BFT) and meat quality traits of the green hams (ham weight loss at first salting, HWLFS; and visible intermuscular fat, VIF). In this study, we evaluated whether a selective genotyping approach previously designed for BFT could identify markers associated with other traits (ADG, FGR, HW, HWLFS, LC and VIF), most of which correlated with BFT. Italian Large White gilts were chosen according to their extreme estimated breeding values for BFT (275 with the most negative and 278 with the most positive EBVs) within a population of about 12,000 sib-tested pigs. A total of 736 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in candidate genes for fat deposition and/or related traits were genotyped. After filtering, a total of 279 SNPs in 234 genes remained for association analyses that were carried out using random residuals (RRs) for the six mentioned traits. Four SNPs in three candidate genes were associated with some of the considered traits. A SNP in the exosome component 1 (EXOSC1) gene and a SNP in the glycogen phosphorylase L (PYGL) gene were associated with HWLFS RRs. Two SNPs within the TBC1 (tre-2/USP6, BUB2, cdc16) domain family, member 1 (TBC1D1) gene were associated with LC RRs and suggestively associated with other performance, carcass and meat traits. Association analysis using six TBC1D1 haplotypes, inferred from four genotyped SNPs within this gene, confirmed the results of the single-marker association study. This study contributes to dissect the biological mechanisms underlying the genetic correlations among BFT, HWLFS and LC, which are critical for the sustainable implementation of tailored selection programs in heavy pigs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Dall'Olio, Stefania","Schiavo, Giuseppina","Gallo, Maurizio","Bovo, Samuele","Bertolini, Francesca","Buttazzoni, Luca","Fontanesi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309809"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Dall'Olio, Stefania"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Council for Agricultural Research and Economics","Italian national association of pig breeders","University of Bologna"],"keyword":["Association study","Back fat thickness","GENE","Meat quality","SNP","Sus scrofa"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"candidate gene markers associated with production carcass and meat quality traits in italian large white pigs identified using a selective genotyping approach","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086713910","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-309809","identifier":[{"id":"85086713910","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-114f378a-f327-4fe5-ae4c-263b2d8dc270"],"keyword":["Association study","Back fat thickness","Gene","Meat quality","SNP","Sus scrofa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-476E697BD02048F9DAAC1A3895233353"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"italian national association of pig breeders","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Italian national association of pig breeders","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Marine Living Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"council for agricultural research and economics","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Council for Agricultural Research and Economics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefania","key":"dalloliopau","last":"Dall'Olio","name":"Dall'Olio, Stefania","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppina","key":"schiavopau","last":"Schiavo","name":"Schiavo, Giuseppina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"gallopau","last":"Gallo","name":"Gallo, Maurizio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuele","key":"bovopau","last":"Bovo","name":"Bovo, Samuele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Francesca","key":"bertolinipau","last":"Bertolini","locid":"a699fbc0-784d-48cf-89d8-6ff32d25056b","name":"Bertolini, Francesca","orcid":"0000-0003-4181-3895","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"buttazzonipau","last":"Buttazzoni","name":"Buttazzoni, Luca","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"fontanesipau","last":"Fontanesi","name":"Fontanesi, Luca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.livsci.2020.104145","issn":["18711413","18780490"],"issn_org":["18711413"],"journal":"Livestock Science","paperid":"104145","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Livestock Science","volume":"240"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086713910"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-114f378a-f327-4fe5-ae4c-263b2d8dc270"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Candidate gene markers associated with production, carcass and meat quality traits in Italian Large White pigs identified using a selective genotyping approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309809","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Runs of homozygosity (ROH) in a diploid organism can be defined as continuous chromosome regions in which all loci have a homozygous genotype. Shared ROH within a livestock population identify chromosome regions in which a reduced haplotype variability produces ROH islands. ROH islands can provide information on hotspot of selection putatively derived from different selection history, genetic events and adaptation to several production systems. In this study we evaluated the distribution of ROH in the genome of a total of 2860 pigs belonging to seven Italian breeds, three commercial breeds (Italian Large White, Italian Duroc and Italian Landrace) and four autochthonous breeds (Apulo-Calabrese, Casertana, Cinta Senese and Nero Siciliano). All animals were genotyped with the Illumina PorcineSNP60 BeadChip array. PLINK software was used to call ROH. The largest number of ROH per animal was observed in the Italian Duroc breed. The mean largest size of ROH was detected in Apulo-Calabrese pigs. Nero Siciliano pigs had the lowest mean number of ROH per animal. Italian Large White pigs had the lowest mean length of ROH. ROH islands were identified in all breeds except in Nero Siciliano. ROH islands spanned from a total of 25.5 (Cinta Senese) to 33.1 Mbp (Italian Landrace) of genomic regions distributed from four to ten autosomes and encompassing from a total of 126 to 262 annotated genes. These selection hotspot regions differed among breeds. Functional inference of the observed ROH islands provided some insights into the mechanisms of adaptation of these pig genetic resources.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Schiavo, Giuseppina","Bovo, Samuele","Bertolini, Francesca","Dall'Olio, Stefania","Nanni Costa, Leonardo","Tinarelli, Silvia","Gallo, Maurizio","Fontanesi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-325428"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fontanesi, Luca"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Italian national association of pig breeders","University of Bologna"],"keyword":["Genetic resource","Genome","Selective sweep","Single nucleotide polymorphism","Sus scrofa"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"runs of homozygosity islands in italian cosmopolitan and autochthonous pig breeds identify selection signatures in the porcine genome","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85089595285","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-325428","identifier":[{"id":"85089595285","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-461579d2-b3a8-4848-b3f3-b80c1de5a8a3"],"keyword":["Genetic resource","Genome","Selective sweep","Single nucleotide polymorphism","Sus scrofa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6BC939109F6C8C3D0C52BB1C7C9F1AD7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Marine Living Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"italian national association of pig breeders","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Italian national association of pig breeders","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppina","key":"schiavopau","last":"Schiavo","name":"Schiavo, Giuseppina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuele","key":"bovopau","last":"Bovo","name":"Bovo, Samuele","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Francesca","key":"bertolinipau","last":"Bertolini","locid":"a699fbc0-784d-48cf-89d8-6ff32d25056b","name":"Bertolini, Francesca","orcid":"0000-0003-4181-3895","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefania","key":"dalloliopau","last":"Dall'Olio","name":"Dall'Olio, Stefania","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leonardo","key":"nannicostapau","last":"Nanni Costa","name":"Nanni Costa, Leonardo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvia","key":"tinarellipau","last":"Tinarelli","name":"Tinarelli, Silvia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"gallopau","last":"Gallo","name":"Gallo, Maurizio","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"fontanesipau","last":"Fontanesi","name":"Fontanesi, Luca","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.livsci.2020.104219","issn":["18711413","18780490"],"issn_org":["18711413"],"journal":"Livestock Science","paperid":"104219","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Livestock Science","volume":"240"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089595285"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-461579d2-b3a8-4848-b3f3-b80c1de5a8a3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Runs of homozygosity islands in Italian cosmopolitan and autochthonous pig breeds identify selection signatures in the porcine genome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-325428","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Casertana is an autochthonous pig breed reared in the Central-South of Italy, mainly in extensive or semi-extensive production systems. A small number of animals are registered to the breed herd-book. The population of this breed is not completely fixed for several exterior traits, including ear size (small vs large), ear bearing (forward vs floppy), presence or absence of wattles and coat colour (black vs slate-grey) that we recorded in a total of 101 pigs from six different farms. All these pigs were also genotyped with the Illumina PorcineSNP60 BeadChip. Then, with the aim to identify DNA markers associated with these traits, we run four genome-wide association studies (GWAS) comparing pigs having different phenotypes for each of the four external traits. Genome-wide fixation index (FST) analyses were run to confirm the results. GEMMA software was used in the GWAS. Single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) associated to the wattle trait were identified on porcine chromosome (SSC) 1 and SSC11. Markers associated to the coat colour trait were located on SSC6, SSC8, SSC14 and SSC15. These chromosome regions were confirmed by the independent FST analyses. FST did not confirm the signals detected for the two ear conformation traits. Candidate genes were identified according to the function of the annotated genes in the detected genome regions. Despite the small number of pigs that could be investigated, this study showed that autochthonous animal genetic resources might be useful to disclose genetic factors affecting traits that are not fixed in a population.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schiavo, Giuseppina","Bovo, Samuele","Tinarelli, Silvia","Bertolini, Francesca","Dall'Olio, Stefania","Gallo, Maurizio","Fontanesi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-310095"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Italian national association of pig breeders","University of Bologna"],"keyword":["Animal genetic resource","Coat colour","Single nucleotide polymorphism","Sus scrofa"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide association analyses for several exterior traits in the autochthonous casertana pig breed","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85074484668","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-310095","identifier":[{"id":"85074484668","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-12528443-4391-4b63-b6f9-1bb78a32f1a2"],"keyword":["Animal genetic resource","Coat colour","Ear conformation","Single nucleotide polymorphism","Sus scrofa","Wattle"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6C4C66B5C9EA166266D8F84C3EDBBB6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Marine Living Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"italian national association of pig breeders","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Italian national association of pig breeders","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppina","key":"schiavopau","last":"Schiavo","name":"Schiavo, Giuseppina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuele","key":"bovopau","last":"Bovo","name":"Bovo, Samuele","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvia","key":"tinarellipau","last":"Tinarelli","name":"Tinarelli, Silvia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"bertolinipau","last":"Bertolini","locid":"a699fbc0-784d-48cf-89d8-6ff32d25056b","name":"Bertolini, Francesca","orcid":"0000-0003-4181-3895","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefania","key":"dalloliopau","last":"Dall'Olio","name":"Dall'Olio, Stefania","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"gallopau","last":"Gallo","name":"Gallo, Maurizio","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"fontanesipau","last":"Fontanesi","name":"Fontanesi, Luca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.livsci.2019.103842","issn":["18711413","18780490"],"issn_org":["18711413"],"journal":"Livestock Science","pages":"103842","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Livestock Science","volume":"230"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074484668"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-12528443-4391-4b63-b6f9-1bb78a32f1a2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Genome-wide association analyses for several exterior traits in the autochthonous Casertana pig breed","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-310095","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Haematological and clinical-biochemical parameters are considered indicators of the physiological/health status of animals and might serve as intermediate phenotypes to link physiological aspects to production and disease resistance traits. The dissection of the genetic variability affecting these phenotypes might be useful to describe the resilience of the animals and to support the usefulness of the pig as animal model. Here, we analysed 15 haematological and 15 clinical-biochemical traits in 843 Italian Large White pigs, via three genome-wide association scan approaches (single-trait, multi-trait and Bayesian). We identified 52 quantitative trait loci (QTLs) associated with 29 out of 30 analysed blood parameters, with the most significant QTL identified on porcine chromosome 14 for basophil count. Some QTL regions harbour genes that may be the obvious candidates: QTLs for cholesterol parameters identified genes (ADCY8, APOB, ATG5, CDKAL1, PCSK5, PRL and SOX6) that are directly involved in cholesterol metabolism; other QTLs highlighted genes encoding the enzymes being measured [ALT (known also as GPT) and AST (known also as GOT)]. Moreover, the multivariate approach strengthened the association results for several candidate genes. The obtained results can contribute to define new measurable phenotypes that could be applied in breeding programs as proxies for more complex traits.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bovo, Samuele","Mazzoni, Gianluca","Bertolini, Francesca","Schiavo, Giuseppina","Galimberti, Giuliano","Gallo, Maurizio","Dall'Olio, Stefania","Fontanesi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-344368"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fontanesi, Luca"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Italian national association of pig breeders","University of Bologna"],"keyword":["Data integration","Functional genomics","Homeostasis","Quantitative trait"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide association studies for 000000000030 haematological and blood clinical biochemical traits in large white pigs reveal genomic regions affecting intermediate phenotypes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-43297-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-344368","identifier":[{"id":"31065004","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85065395679","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6504931","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-854ce3ae-b701-42ec-8876-86d07a02185c"],"keyword":["Agricultural genetics","Data integration","Functional genomics","Homeostasis","Quantitative trait"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83D2E3C4FA6B2BFB57C4641DFBE1D35F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-43297-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/178140882/s41598_019_43297_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Bioinformatics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Bioinformatics, Integrative Systems Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"italian national association of pig breeders","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Italian national association of pig breeders","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuele","key":"bovopau","last":"Bovo","name":"Bovo, Samuele","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianluca","key":"mazzonipau","last":"Mazzoni","locid":"698d1ec9-732a-4410-9377-9e0f146defda","name":"Mazzoni, Gianluca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"bertolinipau","last":"Bertolini","locid":"a699fbc0-784d-48cf-89d8-6ff32d25056b","name":"Bertolini, Francesca","orcid":"0000-0003-4181-3895","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppina","key":"schiavopau","last":"Schiavo","name":"Schiavo, Giuseppina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuliano","key":"galimbertipau","last":"Galimberti","name":"Galimberti, Giuliano","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"gallopau","last":"Gallo","name":"Gallo, Maurizio","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefania","key":"dalloliopau","last":"Dall'Olio","name":"Dall'Olio, Stefania","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"fontanesipau","last":"Fontanesi","name":"Fontanesi, Luca","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31065004"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-019-43297-1","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"7003","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065395679"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-854ce3ae-b701-42ec-8876-86d07a02185c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Genome-wide association studies for 30 haematological and blood clinical-biochemical traits in Large White pigs reveal genomic regions affecting intermediate phenotypes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-344368","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Casertana is a local pig breed mainly raised in Central-South regions of Italy. Pigs of this breed are considered the descendants of the ancient Neapolitan population that largely influenced the constitution of the modern commercial pigs. The pigs of this breed are usually curly-tailed, like several other domestic pig populations. However, Casertana population shows some variability for this trait, including animals having straight tail as observed in wild boars. In this study, we run, for the first time, a genome wide association study (GWAS) comparing the curly tailed (no. = 53) and straight tailed (no. = 19) Casertana pigs to identify genomic regions associated with the tail shape phenotype in Sus scrofa. All animals were genotyped with the Illumina PorcineSNP60 BeadChip v.2. GEMMA software was used in the GWAS for which we were able to correct for stratification in the analysed cohort. A single nucleotide polymorphism (rs81439488), located on porcine chromosome 12, was significantly associated with the investigated trait. This marker is close to the SRY-box 9 (SOX9) gene that encodes for a transcription factor that is required during sequential steps of the chondrocyte differentiation pathway, notochord maintenance and skeletogenesis. As the shape of the tail could be important in relation to the problem of tail biting in pigs, the obtained results might open new perspectives for defining selection programs answering indirectly animal welfare issues. This work demonstrated that autochthonous animal genetic resources might be used to disclose genetic factors affecting peculiar traits by exploiting segregating phenotypes and genetic variability.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bertolini, Francesca","Schiavo, Giuseppina","Tinarelli, Silvia","Santoro, Laura","Utzeri, Valerio Joe","Dall'Olio, Stefania","Costa, Leonardo Nanni","Gallo, Maurizio","Fontanesi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-310897"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fontanesi, Luca"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations","Italian national association of pig breeders","University of Bologna"],"keyword":["Animal genetic resource","Autochthonous breed","GWAS","Morphological trait","SNP","Sus scrofa"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploiting phenotype diversity in a local animal genetic resource identification of a single nucleotide polymorphism associated with the tail shape phenotype in the autochthonous casertana pig breed","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152196767/1_s2.0_S1871141318302348_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-310897","identifier":[{"id":"85052081874","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-14f840a7-5644-455f-ba14-624c96375163"],"keyword":["Animal genetic resource","Autochthonous breed","GWAS","Morphological trait","SNP","Sus scrofa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE2F758D1403B40B50B987E445CBA3F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152196767/1_s2.0_S1871141318302348_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Bio and Health Informatics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"food and agriculture organization of the united nations","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"italian national association of pig breeders","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Italian national association of pig breeders","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Francesca","key":"bertolinipau","last":"Bertolini","locid":"a699fbc0-784d-48cf-89d8-6ff32d25056b","name":"Bertolini, Francesca","orcid":"0000-0003-4181-3895","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppina","key":"schiavopau","last":"Schiavo","name":"Schiavo, Giuseppina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvia","key":"tinarellipau","last":"Tinarelli","name":"Tinarelli, Silvia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"santoropau","last":"Santoro","name":"Santoro, Laura","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Valerio Joe","key":"utzeripau","last":"Utzeri","name":"Utzeri, Valerio Joe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefania","key":"dalloliopau","last":"Dall'Olio","name":"Dall'Olio, Stefania","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leonardo Nanni","key":"costapau","last":"Costa","name":"Costa, Leonardo Nanni","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"gallopau","last":"Gallo","name":"Gallo, Maurizio","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"fontanesipau","last":"Fontanesi","name":"Fontanesi, Luca","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.livsci.2018.08.007","issn":["18711413","18780490"],"issn_org":["18711413"],"journal":"Livestock Science","pages":"148-152","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Livestock Science","volume":"216"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052081874"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-14f840a7-5644-455f-ba14-624c96375163"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Exploiting phenotype diversity in a local animal genetic resource: identification of a single nucleotide polymorphism associated with the tail shape phenotype in the autochthonous Casertana pig breed","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-310897","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) methodologies offer a comprehensive characterization of foodstuffs owing to the possibility to study a sample from different points of view including structural, compositional, functional, morphological etc. aspects. High resolution NMR spectroscopy applied to semi-solid food samples or to extracts in solution is used to determine the foodstuff composition. Here, some features of high resolution NMR methodologies related to food analysis such as quantitative analysis, chemometrics, and use of databases are included. Other NMR methodologies such as relaxometry and imaging described in this chapter give precious information regarding morphology and texture of intact food samples.","author_count":55,"contributors":["Mannina, Luisa","Sobolev, Anatoly Petrovich","Aru, Violetta","Bellomaria, Alessia","Bertocchi, Fabio","Botta, Bruno","Cagliani, Laura Ruth","Caligiani, Augusta","Capozzi, Francesco","Çela, Dorisa","Marincola, Flaminia Cesare","Ciampa, Alessandra","Cocoo, Laura Del","Consonni, Roberto","Corsaro, Carmelo","Delfini, Maurizio","Tullio, Valeria Di","Fanizzio, Francesco Paolo","Gallo, Vito","Ghirga, Francesca","Gianferri, Raffaella","Girellio, Chiara Roberta","Ingallina, Cinzia","Laghi, Luca","Latronico, Mario","Longobardi, Francesco","Luchinat, Claudio","Mallamace, Domenico","Mammi, Stefano","Mandaliti, Walter","Marini, Federico","Mastrorilli, Pietro","Mazzei, Pierluigi","Miccheli, Alfredo","Micozzio, Alessandra","Miloneo, Salvatore","Mucci, Adele","Nepravishta, Ridvan","Paci, Maurizio","Palisi, Angelica","Piccolo, Alessandro","Picone, Gianfranco","Proietti, Noemi","Randazzo, Antonio","Righi, Valeria","Rotondo, Archimede","Salvo, Andrea","Scano, Paola","Scano, Paola","Sciubba, Fabio","Trimigno, Alessia","Tenori, Leonardo","Schievano, Elisabetta","Turano, Paola","Vasi, Sebastiano","Capitani, Donatella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-512523"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributo